11. The nurse is admitting a patient experiencing chest discomfort and shortness of breath, who has  
a history of stroke. When the nurse documents the Nursing diagnosis ―Risk for impaired mobility 
related to history of stroke,‖ the nurse knows which condition to be the risk factor? 
a. Stroke 
b. History of stroke 
c. Chest discomfort 
d. Shortness of breath 
ANS: B 
NURSINGTB.COM 
A two-part risk, Nursing diagnostic statement contains only: (1) the patient‘s identified need or 
problem (i.e., NANDA-I Nursing diagnostic label) and (2) factors indicating vulnerability (i.e., risk  
factors). The risk factor is the history of stroke. The chest discomfort and short ness of breath are 
symptoms of the current problems and would not be documented as potential or 
―risk‖ issues. ―Stroke‖ would be the identified potential problem. 
